==Enemy==
Capy is no longer weighed down by muscle! Becoming a fetid mass of decomposing sludge has its perks: her gains have plummeted and her stats are overall weaker, but she now has a faster attack rate, moves at more than double the speed and warps units far back instead of doing [[Critical Hit|Criticals]]. She revives once with 50% HP like many other zombies, but fortunately cannot burrow. Furthermore, she is immune to both [[Wave Attack|Waves]] and [[Surge Attack|Surges]].

==Strategy==
Normally, Zapy wouldn't be too big of a problem due to her single target, but can become a huge issue if she's either in groups or is paired with support that can punch through your meatshields - especially with the Max # of Deployable Cats restrictions in Cats of the Cosmos' Zombie Outbreaks. Since it ignores immunity to Waves, [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] still retains its phenomenal anti-Zombie performance against her, but you could also try and time a [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Cannon]] with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to either knockback or kill Zapy's support, before rushing the Zapy/Zapies down with [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]]. [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] are extremely potent attackers against Zapy, as their high damage and spammability will make it very easy to tear through Zapy in a few hits.

[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] can tank a hit from this enemy if at a high enough level, and becomes even more effective if you unlock his Warp Immunity [[Talents|Talent]]. Additionally, her lack of Criticals means that [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] works quite well in some cases, though that depends on the enemies supporting Zapy as well as her Warp ability.

