==Trivia==
*Her Japanese name, Tororincho (トロリンチョ), is a portmanteau of とろり ''torori'', meaning "melty" or "gooey", and ''Carpincho'', which is both [[Capy]]'s Japanese name and the Spanish word for [[wikipedia:Capybara|capybara]].
*The "tour of the hot spring hells" in her Japanese description refers to Jigoku Meguri (Hell Tour), a popular tourist activity in the Japanese city of Beppu, which includes seven awe-inspiring hot spring sites known as the [[wikipedia:Hells of Beppu|Hells of Beppu]]; these hot springs are to be observed at a distance due to their extreme heat.
**It can be inferred that she died trying to bathe in one of them during the tour.
*Since Zapy looks slimy and debuts in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 1's [[Zombie Outbreaks]], she may be the source of the purple sludge seen in the [[Media:Bg180.png|rundown facility]] used as a background for some of the CotC Outbreak stages.
**Since some [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] are altered versions of terrestrial enemies (e.g., [[Shibalien]], [[Hyppoh]], [[Bun Bun Symbiote]]), it's possible that Zapy was modified by Aliens enough to gain the Warp ability like most [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], but not enough to gain the Alien trait.

